<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shamsuddin Ahmad Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1835">1835</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shamsuddin Ahmad Khan was nawab of Loharu and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/firozpur-jhirka">Firozpur Jhirka</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, son of the state's founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-bakhsh-khan">Ahmad Bakhsh Khan</a>. In 1835 he was hanged in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> for arranging the murder of William Fraser, the British Resident. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/firozpur">Firozpur</a> Jhirka was confiscated, leaving his family only the small state of Loharu. The poet Ghalib was related to the family by marriage.</p></div>
